# UI design language

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L0 design-language rule (the *look & voice*; code-composition lives elsewhere).

## Use This When

- Building, restyling, or reviewing any **end-user UI surface** (`apps/platform`, `apps/web`, and any consumer-facing pages).
- Deciding color, type, spacing, iconography, motion, or product copy.

## Stop Here If

- Stop once the foundations below answer the design question.

## Descend To

- Component composition / CLI / registries: `/.cursor/rules/shadcn-patterns-required.mdc`
- React composition specifics: `/.cursor/rules/shadcn-patterns-react-ui.mdc`
- Copy that ships as UI strings: `/.cursor/rules/ui-i18n-json-required.mdc` (all visible text is i18n, EN+ES)

## Surface scope (ADR-0005 carve-out)

This language governs **consumer/end-user surfaces** built on shadcn (`@workspace/ui`). The
`apps/author` Payload admin uses `@payloadcms/ui` and is out of scope — do not restyle admin
views to this language.

## The aesthetic in one line

Quiet, neutral, trustworthy. Invisible craft — nothing shouts; everything is balanced,
legible, and calm. Generous whitespace does the work, not color or ornament.

## Tokens are the public API

- Style **only** through the semantic tokens exposed by `@workspace/ui` (`--background`,
  `--foreground`, `--card`, `--muted`, `--accent`, `--border`, `--ring`, `--primary`, …).
- **Never** hardcode hex/oklch/px color or raw shadow values in components. Raw ramps are
  documentation, not the API. Dark theme is the same tokens under `.dark` — get it for free
  by using tokens, never theme-specific literals.

## Visual foundations

- **Color:** strictly **neutral grayscale** (OKLCH neutrals, `baseColor: neutral`). A single
  near-black **primary**. **No brand hue.** The only chromatic colors are `destructive`
  (red) and a blue ramp **reserved for charts**. Don't introduce accent hues for decoration.
- **Type:** the project sans via `--font-sans` for both body and headings; mono for code.
  Headings **semibold (600)** with **tight tracking** (≈ −0.025em); body normal weight at a
  relaxed line-height. Use the Tailwind scale (xs→6xl).
- **Spacing:** Tailwind 0.25rem base. Cards pad **24px**; controls **36px** tall (sm 32,
  lg 40); gaps cluster at 8 / 12 / 16 / 24. Use `gap-*`, never inline ad-hoc margins.
- **Radius:** one knob (`--radius`); everything derives — inputs/buttons `md`, cards `xl`,
  badges/avatars/switches fully round. Soft, never sharp; never pill except badges.
- **Backgrounds:** **flat solid color.** No gradients, textures, patterns, or baked-in hero
  imagery. Calm negative space instead.
- **Borders:** hairline **1px** in `--border` on nearly every surface (cards, inputs,
  separators). This is the system's defining texture.
- **Shadows:** restrained — `shadow-xs` on inputs/outline buttons, `shadow-sm` on cards,
  `shadow-2xl` only on overlays/dialogs. No colored or glowing shadows.
- **Focus rings:** a **3px `--ring` ring** (≈50% opacity) plus a border-color shift — the
  signature interaction cue. Invalid fields ring in `destructive`.
- **Hover/press:** subtle. Solid buttons → ~90% fill opacity; ghost/outline → fill with
  `--accent`; links underline. Slight opacity dip on press. No scale-up, no bounce.
- **Motion:** minimal and fast — ~150ms ease on color/box-shadow/transform; accordion/dialog
  tweens only. **No decorative or looping motion.**
- **Cards:** `--card` surface, 1px border, `radius-xl`, `shadow-sm`, 24px padding,
  header/content/footer stacked with a 24px gap. The quiet, uniform workhorse container.

## Iconography

- **Lucide only** (`iconLibrary: lucide`). 24×24 grid, **1.5px stroke**, round caps/joins,
  no fill, `stroke="currentColor"` so icons inherit text color. Render ~16px in controls,
  18–20px in nav. Never mix icon sets; never use emoji or unicode glyphs as icons.

## Content & copy

- **Sentence case everywhere** — headings, buttons, labels, menu items ("Create project,"
  not "Create Project"). Proper nouns excepted.
- Address the reader as **"you"**; imperative mood for actions.
- **Buttons:** short verbs ("Save changes," "Cancel," "Continue"). Destructive is blunt
  ("Delete").
- **Descriptions:** one calm supporting sentence in `--muted-foreground` under a title.
- **Placeholders/demo data:** realistic but generic. **No emoji** in product UI. Numbers
  shown plainly with a small delta line when relevant.
- Voice: understated, precise, a little dry — trustworthy over playful. (All visible strings
  still go through i18n, EN+ES — see the i18n rule.)

## Avoid

Bluish-purple gradients · emoji · colored left-border "callout" cards · glowing shadows ·
pill-shaped everything · decorative/looping motion · hardcoded color/shadow literals in
components · accent hues used for decoration.
